# Commercial S11.2 R15.4 source/runtime access contract

## Classification

`SOURCE_RUNTIME_ACCESS_IDENTITY_CONFLATION`

R15.3 proved that `SupplementaryGroups=chatops` is loaded by systemd and is
required to traverse the protected `chatops:chatops:2770` parents containing
the canonical Application runtime virtual environment. The remaining access
failure was not a missing group: the Control checkout was legitimately
materialized under `umask 077`, leaving its executable source file owned by
`chatops` with mode `0700`. A root process without `CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE` cannot use
the absent group bits even when `chatops` is supplementary.

## Corrected identity boundary

Source validation is performed as `chatops`. Mode `0700` is explicitly valid,
and no repository owner, group, mode, ACL or sudoers rule is changed.

The systemd controller continues to execute the installed root-owned copy at
`/usr/local/bin/tu1nz_adult_public_s11_2_control.sh`. Its runtime preflight and
natural `observe` path verify a root-owned runtime manifest plus installed
controller, gate, service and timer artefacts by SHA-256, owner, group and
explicit install mode. Neither path reads or executes the Control checkout.

The Application checkout remains bound independently by its exact commit,
tree and clean status because it owns the canonical runtime interpreter. This
preserves the previous Application fail-closed integrity check without
reintroducing a Control checkout dependency.

The Application virtual environment remains the existing canonical runtime
interpreter because `psycopg` is intentionally installed there rather than in
system Python. `SupplementaryGroups=chatops` therefore remains necessary for
parent traversal, but it grants no new source-file access when a file is mode
`0700`.

## Regression and simulation

The source-only simulator reproduces the old direct-repository failure, proves
owner-context source access under `umask 077`, verifies explicit `0755` runtime
installation and hash binding, rejects missing/mismatched/non-executable
copies and repository-bound `ExecStart`, executes the installed controller
without exit 126, and restores prior runtime bytes, modes and absence state
without touching source permissions.

R15.4 performs no server installation and no Canary retry. Public WMS, real
acquisition and its existing baseline remain unchanged. Human acceptance stays
deferred, and Adult media, AVS, payments, publishing, Controlled Beta and
production remain closed.
